# Frequency (native) settings. Copy to frequency.ini next to where you start the game, or point
# FREQ_CONFIG at a file. An environment variable of the same name overrides a line here.

# Disc image and memory card folder.
#FREQ_DISC=Frequency (USA).iso
#FREQ_MC=memcard

# Display: frame rate 60 or 120; resolution factor (1 = PS2, 6 = 4K); 16:9 widescreen (1 = on).
#FREQ_FPS=120
#FREQ_SCALE=6
#FREQ_WIDESCREEN=1
# PS5: FREQ_SCALE defaults to what covers the TV's lines (5 on a 4K set); FREQ_FPS=120 suits a TV
# that the log shows at 119880 mHz. Linux: FREQ_GFX=vulkan draws with Vulkan (a -DPS2GFX_VULKAN=ON build).
#FREQ_GFX=vulkan
# With FREQ_SCALE, lines, points and the feedback blur keep the PS2's size: on (default), or off for
# one-pixel lines and a sharper blur.
#FREQ_SCALE_EFFECTS=off
# Texture filtering: enhanced (default: the game's mip levels with 16x anisotropic filtering, no
# shimmer on far tunnel walls) or original (the top level only, as before).
#FREQ_TEX_FILTER=original
# Colour depth of the Vulkan renderer (PS5): full (default: 16-bit pictures keep 8 bits a channel, no
# banding in glows and trails) or original (5 bits a channel, as the PS2 stores them). OpenGL is always full.
#FREQ_COLOR_DEPTH=original
# Anti-aliasing of edges (FXAA on the finished frame): off (default) or on. It also softens HUD text a
# little and can ripple near-flat edges when the picture is scaled up.
#FREQ_AA=on

# Latency, in ms. Audio and video offsets play the sound and draw the picture that much later than
# the game judges (negative: earlier). The input offset judges your presses that much earlier: the
# calibration sets it (Options > Game Options, press Square, tap any button with the 12 clicks;
# Triangle cancels) and saves it here. A positive video offset also delays catch effects with the
# picture; a negative one cannot show them early. All three are on the remaster's settings too
# (Options > Game Options, press Circle), in 5 ms steps from -250 to 250: the video and input
# offsets apply from the next song, the audio offset from the next start. To line up a TV, play a
# song and move VIDEO OFFSET until the gems reach the catcher on the beat you hear.
#FREQ_AUDIO_OFFSET_MS=0
#FREQ_VIDEO_OFFSET_MS=0
#FREQ_INPUT_OFFSET_MS=0

# Assists, off by default. No fail: running out of energy does not stop the song, but a song that
# ran out still ends as a fail, with no progress or high score saved (1 = on).
#FREQ_NO_FAIL=1
# Timing window: the catch window times this (1.0 = original, 1.5 or 2.0 wider).
#FREQ_TIMING_WINDOW=1.5
# Unlock all: every arena and stage open from the start, as the game's own cheat opens them; unlike
# the cheat, progress and high scores still save (1 = on).
#FREQ_UNLOCK_ALL=1
# Auto-pause, on by default: a song pauses itself, as with Start, when a player's controller
# disconnects, and on the PS5 when the PS button or a system overlay covers the game or the console
# wakes from rest mode. Never in network play (0 = off).
#FREQ_AUTOPAUSE=0

# Practice mode: every song is a practice run, the game's own practice mode (no juice drain; no
# score or progress saved). Select restarts the song at once, and so does Restart in the pause menu,
# without its confirmation. A speed under 1 or a loop turns it on.
#FREQ_PRACTICE=1
# Practice speed, 0.5 to 1 (or 50 to 100 percent): the song plays slower at the same pitch.
#FREQ_PRACTICE_SPEED=0.75
# Practice loop, repeated until you quit or restart: bars (9-16), or phrases, the song's sections
# as the HUD's song-position blocks show them (p3 or p3-4). Counted from 1.
#FREQ_PRACTICE_LOOP=9-16

# Sample playback interpolation: gaussian (default, the console's), linear, cubic, or sinc (8 taps).
#FREQ_SPU_INTERP=sinc

# HUD at the screen edges in 16:9 (1 = on; needs FREQ_WIDESCREEN=1).
#FREQ_HUD_EDGES=1
# Strength of the motion trails (score text trails, feedback blur): 1 = original, 0.5, 0 = off.
#FREQ_TRAILS=0.5
# Player colours (gems, catcher, pointer, lane, HUD): original, or cb for colours that stay
# distinct with red-green colour blindness.
#FREQ_GEM_PALETTE=cb

# The DualSense light bar shows each player's colour (FREQ_GEM_PALETTE's when cb), pulsing on the
# beat during a song and flashing on a captured section (1 = on, default; 0 leaves the bar alone).
#FREQ_LIGHTBAR=0
# On the PS5, L2 or R2 clicks at its press point when it plays a lane, through the adaptive
# triggers (1 = on, default).
#FREQ_TRIGGERS=0
# Online play, up to 4 players on up to 4 machines, free: no account and no paid server. In the
# game, Multiplayer > ONLINE picks HOST or JOIN and a code of three words, and shows the room's
# players; the settings below open a room at start instead. Every machine sets the same room code;
# pick a few words nobody would guess, since anyone with the code can join. One machine is the host
# (FREQ_ONLINE_HOST=1): the songs it starts in Solo or Multiplayer (not remixes or the tutorial)
# start on every machine in the room, and each guest plays one player with its first controller.
# Guests wait in the menus; the console shows a notification when a machine joins or leaves.
#FREQ_ONLINE_ROOM=purple tunnel friday
#FREQ_ONLINE_HOST=1
# The last room Multiplayer > ONLINE opened, for one press there to open it again (these do not open
# a room at start).
#FREQ_ONLINE_LAST_ROOM=ace bird cat
#FREQ_ONLINE_LAST_HOST=1
# The name the others see for this machine's player (up to 12 characters).
#FREQ_ONLINE_NAME=Lefty
# The UDP port (host default 47125, guest any free port). Most home routers let the machines reach
# each other without help; if they cannot, forward this port on the host's router to the host.
#FREQ_ONLINE_PORT=47125
# A guest can skip the meeting and name the host's address (its public IP and port, or its LAN
# address at home).
#FREQ_ONLINE_PEER=203.0.113.7:47125
# Where the machines meet: an ntfy server (default https://ntfy.sh, free, no account; the topic is
# made from the room code, and what is posted there is signed with it), or off with
# FREQ_ONLINE_PEER. The STUN server tells each machine its public address (off to skip).
#FREQ_ONLINE_SIGNAL=https://ntfy.sh
#FREQ_ONLINE_STUN=stun.l.google.com:19302

# 5.1 sound (1 = on), on an output that takes it; otherwise stereo as before.
#FREQ_SURROUND=1
# Spatial mix (1 = on; needs FREQ_SURROUND=1): each instrument plays from its lane in the tunnel,
# the track you are on in front and the others around you, turning as you change tracks. Sound
# effects, reverb, and the backing parts stay spread over the speakers as in plain 5.1.
#FREQ_SPATIAL=1

# Custom songs. FREQ_SONGS is a folder of song folders with files at their game paths (for example
# mysong/levels/mysong/mysongf1_c.mid), and they replace or add to the disc's files; the image is
# not changed. host/io/songs.py unpacks a disc song into a song folder and lists what a new song
# needs. The PS5 default is songs in the title folder.
#FREQ_SONGS=songs

# Bonus songs, on by default: BT's Godspeed and Kareem Caines' Scratchotronic, finished songs on the
# disc that the game never lists, play as a sixth song of stage 4 and stage 1. They open with the
# secret songs (Expert finished, or FREQ_UNLOCK_ALL) and save high scores like any song; progress
# toward a stage does not count them (0 = off).
#FREQ_BONUS_SONGS=0
# Fast boot, on by default: from the second start the memory card check and the Sony screen go by
# without their waits and fades, and the intro movie is skipped. A missing card is still reported.
# The first start writes FREQ_BOOTED=1 here; remove that line to see the full boot again (0 = off).
#FREQ_FAST_BOOT=0

# A look over the finished frame: off (default), bloom (a light glow around the neon), or crt
# (scanlines on each of the PS2's lines). A change applies at once.
#FREQ_FILTER=bloom
# Photo mode has no setting. Pause a song and click the touchpad (or R3). The left stick orbits the
# camera, the right stick zooms, Cross saves a PNG of the screen to photos/ (on the PS5
# /app0/photos, with a notification of the file), and Circle or the touchpad goes back to the pause
# menu.

# Every setting above except the disc, memory card, renderer, songs folder, practice loop and
# online keys is also on the remaster's settings page (Options > Game Options, press Circle), a
# list in sections. Up and Down pick a setting, L1 and R1 jump to the previous or next section,
# Left and Right change it and save it here at once, and Circle or Triangle closes the page. The
# panel under the list explains the setting and shows whether it takes effect from the next start
# or the next song. The keys below are on the page too, except the board code.
# Automatic updates on the PS5, on by default: each start looks for a newer build of the remaster
# and downloads it for the next start (0 = off).
#FREQ_UPDATE=0
# HD textures: a folder of replacement textures (host/gfx/ps2gfx/src/TexReplace.h describes the
# files). Empty or unset is off. The page's HD TEXTURES row sets hd in the working directory
# (/app0/hd on the PS5).
#FREQ_TEX_REPLACE=hd
# Reduce flashing: the white flash of each caught gem at full strength (0, default), half (0.5),
# or none (1).
#FREQ_REDUCE_FLASH=1
# Watch mode: the game plays every song perfectly by itself, with no score or progress saved, as
# a jukebox with the visuals or a demo for guests. Not in network play (1 = on).
#FREQ_WATCH=1
# How early the beat rumble starts, in ms (default 90, tuned for the DualShock 2's motors; the
# page offers 0 to 180 in 10 ms steps). Lower it if the pulse lands after the beat.
#FREQ_RUMBLE_LEAD_MS=60

# Best runs: every solo song is recorded, and a new high score keeps the run in replays/ in the
# title folder (one per song and difficulty). Square on the results screen plays it back.
# FREQ_GHOST=1 shows the kept run's score at the same point of the song, the number under yours.
#FREQ_GHOST=1
# Achievements (25) are listed in achievements.txt in the title folder; each pops a notification.
# A friends board: machines with the same board code share their best score per song, through
# ntfy.sh as online play does (FREQ_ONLINE_SIGNAL applies; the name is FREQ_ONLINE_NAME, or the
# Freq's name); Multiplayer > SCOREBOARD sets the code. Anyone with the code can post any score,
# so give it to friends only. A notification shows your rank after each new best; a post goes out at
# most every 6 minutes.
#FREQ_BOARD=green tunnel scores

# Logs and crash reports have no setting. frequency.log in the title folder (beside this file on
# Linux) is the log of this run. Each start moves the last run's log to
# logs/frequency-<date>-<time>.log, and a crash writes logs/crash-<date>-<time>.txt (the build, the
# signal, the registers and stack, and the end of the log). The newest 10 of each stay; older ones
# are deleted. After a crash the next start shows a notification.
# Send report (on the settings page) sends the last run's crash report, or this run's log, to an
# ntfy topic (free, with no account) as up to 24000 bytes in messages of at most 3800, with tokens,
# keys, room codes, and board codes removed. Open https://ntfy.sh/<topic> (or subscribe to the
# topic in the ntfy app) within 12 hours to read it. The first start writes a random topic here.
#FREQ_REPORT_TOPIC=frequency-0123456789abcdef
# The ntfy server reports go to (default https://ntfy.sh).
#FREQ_REPORT_SERVER=https://ntfy.sh
# A crash at start, to try the crash report (1 = on; remove the line afterwards).
#FREQ_TEST_CRASH=1
